feat: append-only planner evidence ledger for reconstructable trajectories

Every planning attempt is now persistently recorded with runID, taskID,
cycleID, attempt number, repair classification, raw model output, validator
errors, and compiled arguments, attributed via an explicit run-to-task
registry instead of latest-goal heuristics. The schema experiment harness
adds per-run argument-preservation chains (raw -> compiled -> executed ->
stdout) and plan-snapshot history so initial plans are never overwritten by
replans. Reporting-only: no agent behavior depends on the ledger.

